nina park: Quick note — onboarding a customer with the Next + LlamaIndex starter. Hitting a repeat-401 problem on Edge; looks like the sample's fetch helper loses auth when the SDK retries.
omar: Thanks. Repro: deploy starter, call /api/assist -> initial request 401 (token rotate), client retries but Authorization header missing and it retries indefinitely. Seen on both Vercel Edge and our private Edge image.
li wei: I traced it to @redwood/sdk-edge retry path. It reconstructs a Request without merging runtime-provided headers (ephemeral auth). SDK-js keeps headers intact.
nina park: For the immediate fix, I've added a defensive helper in the starter to ensure Authorization is present for every attempt. README updated under "Edge gotchas".
omar: Helper snippet added to repo (samples/starter-next/src/lib/authFetch.js):
```js
export async function authFetch(input, init = {}) {
  const req = input instanceof Request ? input : new Request(input, init);
  const headers = new Headers(req.headers);
  if (globalThis.__SAMPLE_TOKEN) headers.set('authorization', `Bearer ${globalThis.__SAMPLE_TOKEN}`);
  return fetch(new Request(req.url, { method: req.method, headers, body: await req.clone().arrayBuffer() }));
}
```
li wei: I also added a unit test in sdk-edge to assert headers are forwarded on retry and an eval-harness scenario that simulates token expiry in CI: `eval-harness run --scenario edge-auth-flaky --sample starter-next`.
qa-bot: CI job samples/e2e/edge-auth-flaky scheduled for branch fix/auth-retry-2205.
nina park: We'll publish a patch version of the starter with the workaround and bump sdk-edge once the header-copy change lands. Also adding a one-line triage note to the SE onboarding checklist: "If Edge starter shows repeated 401s, ensure starter helper sets Authorization explicitly or upgrade sdk-edge."
omar: Filed infra ticket 3589 for the sdk-edge fix and linked the starter PR.
li wei: PR 3590 includes the retry header merge and a regression test. Once merged we can remove the workaround from the starter.
nina park: Thanks — this should reduce onboarding friction for new teams using the Next + LlamaIndex templates.
